EndDraw must not fail for an ID2D1CommandList target.

WHAT THE USER SEES: in After Effects 2025, Composition > New Composition pops
"direct2d drawbot error. HRESULT: -2147467263" and no composition is created.
The app is otherwise usable, so this blocks the single most important action in it.

ROOT CAUSE: -2147467263 is 0x80004001 = E_NOTIMPL. AE's composition viewer draws by
RECORDING into an ID2D1CommandList (the standard "record now, replay later" D2D
pattern) rather than drawing straight to a render target. Wine's
d2d_device_context_EndDraw refused that target type outright, so the viewer's very
first draw failed and the drawbot gave up.

THE FIX: a command-list target records rather than renders, so there is nothing to
present at EndDraw -- it simply ends recording, and the app finalises the list with
ID2D1CommandList::Close() (already implemented). Returning the accumulated error
code, exactly as the normal path does, is the correct behaviour.

MEASURED (2026-07-31, staged as a single dll on runtime 11.10-19, user-confirmed):
  * New Composition SUCCEEDS -- the error dialog is gone;
  * command-list use goes from 2 to 301 Close() calls in one session, i.e. AE
    exercises the path hard once it is no longer blocked;
  * the Composition panel changes from white to black, because AE's paint pipeline
    now runs to completion instead of aborting partway.

SCOPE -- READ BEFORE EXTENDING THIS: this patch is deliberately ONLY the EndDraw
fix. A much larger companion change (an ID2D1CommandSink that replays a recorded
list onto a device context, wiring up DrawImage, ~400 lines) was written and
compile-tested, but instrumentation proved AE NEVER executes it: 48+ lists close in
state OPEN with real content, yet there are ZERO Stream() calls, ZERO
DrawImage-with-a-command-list, ZERO "Unhandled image" and ZERO "Only image brushes
with bitmaps" -- AE records healthy lists and consumes them by no d2d path at all.
Shipping unverified code in a release runtime is not worth the risk, so that work is
parked, with its full measured result, in
patches/unverified/README-d2d1-command-list.md. Do not resurrect it believing it
fixes After Effects; it does not.

STILL OPEN AFTER THIS (not caused by it): composition CONTENT does not render --
shapes drawn into a comp are invisible and the panel is black. That is a separate
bug and is NOT the command-list path.

ORDERING: must apply AFTER neutron-zzz4-d2d1-batched-devicecontext-state, which adds
the d2d_device_context_release_state() call used as leading context here. "zzz9"
sorts after "zzz4" under the system locale's collation, which ignores punctuation
(see preserved-fixes/harnesses/check-patch-order.py -- an earlier patch shipped
against the wrong base because "zzz2-" collates BEFORE "zzz-").

--- a/dlls/d2d1/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/device.c
@@ -3143,16 +3143,18 @@
 
     d2d_device_context_release_state(context);
 
-    if (context->target.type == D2D_TARGET_COMMAND_LIST)
-    {
-        FIXME("Unimplemented for command list target.\n");
-        return E_NOTIMPL;
-    }
-
     if (tag1)
         *tag1 = context->error.tag1;
     if (tag2)
         *tag2 = context->error.tag2;
+
+    /* NEUTRON: a command-list target records rather than renders, so there is
+     * nothing to present -- ending the draw just ends recording, and the app
+     * finalises the list with ID2D1CommandList::Close(). This used to return
+     * E_NOTIMPL, which killed After Effects' composition viewer on its very
+     * first draw ("direct2d drawbot error. HRESULT: -2147467263"). */
+    if (context->target.type == D2D_TARGET_COMMAND_LIST)
+        return context->error.code;
 
     if (context->ops && context->ops->device_context_present)
     {
